NetApp Interview Answer

SATA (Serial Advanced Technology Attachment) is a storage interface used to connect HDDs and SSDs to a computer or storage system. Traditional SATA SSDs are limited to about 550 MB/s because of the SATA interface. Modern NVMe SSDs use PCIe instead of SATA, providing much higher throughput and lower latency for performance-sensitive workloads.

